---
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Header from "../../../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../../../components/Footer.astro";
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import fructoseImage from '../../../assets/images/fruits-fructose.jpg';
---
<BaseLayout title="Fructose Intolerance Checker - Self-Test - FoodCheck" description="Bloating or discomfort after fruit or honey? Our free fructose intolerance checker helps identify possible malabsorption patterns. Educational tool only." breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Tools', href: '/tools' }, { label: 'Fructose Intolerance Checker', href: '/tools/fructose-intolerance-test' }]}">
<Header /><main>
<section class="pt-16 pb-8 md:pt-24 px-4 sm:px-6 max-w-6xl mx-auto">
<div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto text-center">
<h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-900 leading-none mb-4">Fructose Intolerance Checker</h1>
<p class="text-lg text-slate-500 max-w-lg mx-auto">5 questions to explore possible fructose malabsorption. Educational tool only.</p>
</div>
<div class="mt-8 max-w-2xl mx-auto"><Image src={fructoseImage} alt="Fresh fruits and honey containing natural fructose" class="w-full h-auto rounded-xl" width={800} height={450} loading="lazy" format="webp" /></div>
</section>
<section class="pb-16 md:pb-24 px-4 sm:px-6 max-w-6xl mx-auto"><div class="max-w-xl mx-auto">
<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-4 text-center">Take the Assessment</h2>
<div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-2xl shadow-sm p-6 sm:p-8">
<div class="space-y-6" id="fructose-quiz"><p class="text-center text-slate-400 text-sm">Select your answers to get your result.</p></div>
<div id="fructose-result" class="hidden"></div>
</div><div class="mt-8 bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 rounded-xl p-4 text-xs text-amber-800">Not a medical diagnosis. Consult your GP or a dietitian.</div>
<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900 mt-10 mb-3">How Does This Fructose Checker Work?</h2>
<p class="text-slate-600 text-sm mb-4">This fructose intolerance checker explores your symptoms after eating fruit, honey, and high-fructose foods. Fructose malabsorption occurs when the small intestine cannot efficiently absorb fructose, leading to bloating, gas, and altered bowel habits. According to research published in <em>Nutrients</em>, fructose malabsorption affects approximately <strong>30–40% of the population</strong> in Western countries.</p>
<p class="text-slate-600 text-sm mb-4">A hydrogen breath test for fructose, available through your GP, is the gold standard for confirming fructose malabsorption.</p>
<h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900 mt-6 mb-2">What Is Fructose Malabsorption?</h3>
<p class="text-slate-600 text-sm mb-4">Fructose malabsorption occurs when the small intestine's fructose transporters (GLUT5) cannot absorb fructose efficiently. Unabsorbed fructose reaches the large intestine, where bacteria ferment it, producing gas and drawing in water. Unlike hereditary fructose intolerance (a rare genetic condition), fructose malabsorption is common and not dangerous, but can significantly affect quality of life.</p>
<h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900 mt-6 mb-2">Which Foods Are Highest in Fructose?</h3>
<p class="text-slate-600 text-sm mb-4">Foods with excess fructose over glucose are most problematic: apples, pears, mangoes, watermelon, honey, agave syrup, and high-fructose corn syrup. Foods where fructose equals glucose (bananas, berries, oranges) are usually well-tolerated. The <strong>Monash University</strong> low FODMAP app is a useful reference for fructose content in specific foods and portion sizes.</p>
<h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900 mt-6 mb-2">What Should You Do If Results Suggest Fructose Intolerance?</h3>
<p class="text-slate-600 text-sm mb-4">Try reducing high-fructose foods for 2–4 weeks, then reintroduce one at a time. Many people tolerate small amounts of fructose, especially when eaten with glucose-containing foods. See our <a href="/blog/low-fodmap-foods" class="text-brand-600 hover:text-brand-700 underline">Low FODMAP Food List</a> for specific fructose content guidance.</p>
<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900 mt-10 mb-3">What Resources Can Help You Learn More?</h2>
<div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3">
<a href="/blog/low-fodmap-foods" class="block bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 rounded-lg p-4 hover:border-brand-300 transition-colors no-underline"><h3 class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-900 mb-1">Low FODMAP Food List</h3><p class="text-xs text-slate-500">High and low fructose foods reference guide.</p></a>
<a href="/tools/food-diary" class="block bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 rounded-lg p-4 hover:border-brand-300 transition-colors no-underline"><h3 class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-900 mb-1">Food Diary</h3><p class="text-xs text-slate-500">Track fruit intake and fructose symptoms.</p></a>
<a href="/guides/test-guide" class="block bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 rounded-lg p-4 hover:border-brand-300 transition-colors no-underline"><h3 class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-900 mb-1">Testing Guide</h3><p class="text-xs text-slate-500">Hydrogen breath tests for fructose malabsorption.</p></a>
<a href="/blog/elimination-diet-guide" class="block bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 rounded-lg p-4 hover:border-brand-300 transition-colors no-underline"><h3 class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-900 mb-1">Elimination Diet Guide</h3><p class="text-xs text-slate-500">Structured protocol to confirm fructose triggers.</p></a>
</div>
</div></section>
</main><Footer /></BaseLayout>
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebApplication",
  "name": "Fructose Intolerance Checker",
  "url": "https://foodintolerancecheck.com/tools/fructose-intolerance-test",
  "description": "Free online fructose malabsorption self-assessment tool. Explore whether your fruit-related symptoms suggest fructose intolerance.",
  "applicationCategory": "HealthApplication",
  "operatingSystem": "All",
  "offers": { "@type": "Offer", "price": "0", "priceCurrency": "USD" }
}
</script>
<script is:inline src="/js/fructose-checker.js"></script>
